MODEL WATCH #56 — Thursday, September 17, 2026

1. SABLE-3.1
Point release; same price. Long-context recall at 400k goes from 71 to 89 on our needle set, and refusals on benign enterprise text drop from 2.1% to 0.4%. Composite 85.1 (from 83.9). Upgrade unless you pinned a version for a reason.

2. THE OPEN VS. PROPRIETARY GAP, BY TASK FAMILY
Best proprietary vs. best open model on each family, Q3:

  Family          Best proprietary       Best open           Gap
  Extraction      Sable-3.1   96.0       Ferrite-70B  94.1    1.9
  Classification  Sable-3.1   97.2       Ferrite-70B  96.0    1.2
  Tool use        Sable-3.1   97.4       Ferrite-70B  95.0    2.4
  Reasoning       Lodestone-R2 94.8      Ferrite-70B  68.2   26.6
  Long context    Sable-3.1   89.0       Ferrite-70B  74.5   14.5

For the first three families the open model is a rational default. For the last two, it is not.

3. ARGENT UNDERCUTS ON FERRITE-70B
$0.55 / $1.70, five cents under Kestrel on output. First price competition on an open 70B; we expect Nimbus to list it within the week.

4. PRICE CHANGES THIS WEEK
  Argent, Ferrite-70B: new, $0.55 / $1.70
  Argent batch tier: new, -50%, 24-hour window
  Halcyon Vision 3: -30% per image

